<p>I don't mean it's not professional, I mean it doesn't sound like something a regular Joe would ever think to say. He swings between conversational (&quot;Day started normal enough&quot;), flowery excess (&quot;something beyond mortal terror on his face&quot;) and over-precision (&quot;and his fingers were severed between the door and its frame&quot;). The guy doesn't have a consistent &quot;voice.&quot;</p>

							</div>

								
